{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X4i7r38Yxvdfne3JP5Byxy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Task entry point for taiga-back. Run `make` or `make help` to list targets.\n# All Python commands run from the .venv virtualenv created by `make setup`.\n\nSHELL := /bin/bash\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\nVENV := .venv\nPY := $(VENV)/bin/python\nPYTEST := $(VENV)/bin/pytest\nFLAKE8 := $(VENV)/bin/flake8\n\n# Same coverage command as the CI workflow before the harness.\nCOVERAGE_OMIT := *tests*,*commands*,*migrations*,*admin*,*.jinja,*dashboard*,*settings*,*wsgi*,*questions*,*documents*\n\n# flake8 rules enforced by the gates: syntax errors and invalid comparisons only.\n# The full rule set from setup.cfg (`make lint-full`) reports existing violations\n# in old code, see docs/harness/log.md.\nLINT_GATE_SELECT := E9,F63,F7\n\n.PHONY: help setup venv deps hooks db-up db-down db-migrate db-reset dev worker \\\n        test test-unit lint lint-full migrations-check check-fast check\n\nhelp: ## Show this help\n\t@grep -E '^[a-zA-Z_-]+:.*?## ' $(MAKEFILE_LIST) | \\\n\t\tawk 'BEGIN {FS = \":.*?## \"}; {printf \"  \\033[36m%-17s\\033[0m %s\\n\", $$1, $$2}'\n\nsetup: deps hooks db-up db-migrate ## Install dependencies, install the git hook, start PostgreSQL and apply migrations\n\n$(PY):\n\t@if command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n\t\tuv venv --seed --python 3.10 $(VENV); \\\n\telif command -v python3.10 >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n\t\tpython3.10 -m venv $(VENV); \\\n\telse \\\n\t\tpython3 -m venv $(VENV); \\\n\tfi\n\t@$(PY) -c 'import sys; v = sys.version_info[:2]; print(\"WARNING: .venv uses Python %d.%d, the project pins 3.10\" % v) if v != (3, 10) else None'\n\nvenv: $(PY) ## Create the .venv virtualenv with Python 3.10 (uses uv when available)\n\ndeps: $(PY) ## Install requirements.txt and requirements-devel.txt into .venv (like scripts/install)\n\t$(PY) -m pip install --upgrade pip wheel setuptools\n\t$(PY) -m pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-devel.txt\n\nhooks: ## Install the pre-push git hook (.githooks/pre-push) that runs `make check-fast`\n\t@git config core.hooksPath .githooks || \\\n\t\techo \"WARNING: could not install the git hook (no .git or read-only git metadata)\"\n\ndb-up: ## Start PostgreSQL from compose.yaml (skipped when CI is set: CI has its own service)\n\t@if [ -n \"$$CI\" ]; then \\\n\t\techo \"CI is set: using the PostgreSQL service of the CI job\"; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\tdocker compose up -d --wait postgres; \\\n\tfi\n\ndb-down: ## Stop the compose services (data stays in the postgres-data volume)\n\tdocker compose --profile async down\n\ndb-migrate: ## Apply migrations to the local development database (skipped in CI)\n\t@if [ -n \"$$CI\" ]; then \\\n\t\techo \"CI is set: tests create their own database, skipping\"; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(PY) manage.py migrate --noinput; \\\n\tfi\n\ndb-reset: db-up ## DESTROYS local data: recreate the database with admin/123123 and sample data (regenerate.sh)\n\tPGPASSWORD=taiga PATH=\"$(CURDIR)/$(VENV)/bin:$$PATH\" ./regenerate.sh -y < /dev/null\n\ndev: db-up ## Run the API on http://localhost:8000 with settings/config.py (copied from the dev example if missing)\n\t@test -f settings/config.py || cp settings/config.py.dev.example settings/config.py\n\tDJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=settings.config $(PY) manage.py runserver\n\nworker: ## Run a Celery worker with beat (needs CELERY_ENABLED=True in settings/config.py and `docker compose --profile async up -d`)\n\tDJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=settings.config $(VENV)/bin/celery -A taiga.celery worker -B -l INFO\n\n# The whole suite needs a fresh test database (--create-db): transactional tests\n# flush all tables on teardown, which removes rows created by data migrations\n# (for example the system users of taiga/hooks). A reused database breaks the\n# tests/integration/test_hooks_* files. Unit tests do not need that data, so the\n# fast gate keeps --reuse-db.\ntest: db-up ## Run the whole test suite (one test: .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_slug.py -k <name>)\n\t$(PYTEST) --create-db\n\ntest-unit: db-up ## Run the unit tests only (tests/unit)\n\t$(PYTEST) tests/unit --reuse-db -rA --tb=short\n\nlint: ## Run flake8 with the rules enforced by the gates (syntax errors, invalid comparisons)\n\t$(FLAKE8) --select=$(LINT_GATE_SELECT) .\n\nlint-full: ## Run flake8 with the full setup.cfg rules (fails today on existing code, see docs/harness/log.md)\n\t$(FLAKE8) .\n\nmigrations-check: ## Fail when a model change has no migration\n\tDJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=tests.config $(PY) manage.py makemigrations --check --dry-run\n\ncheck-fast: lint test-unit ## Fast gate: lint plus unit tests. Run before every push\n\ncheck: lint db-up migrations-check ## Full gate, what CI runs: lint, migrations check, whole suite with coverage\n\t$(VENV)/bin/coverage run --source=taiga --omit='$(COVERAGE_OMIT)' \\\n\t\t-m pytest -v --tb=native --pythonwarnings=default --create-db\n# Local development\n\nThe API runs on the host in a Python 3.10 virtualenv (`.venv`). PostgreSQL runs in Docker from `compose.yaml`. RabbitMQ is optional.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Needs a human.** Which local setup do developers use today (a local PostgreSQL, the taiga-docker repository, something else), and should `compose.yaml` also start RabbitMQ by default and taiga-events?\n> Why it matters and how to do it: https://docs.unwritten.sh/harness/requirements/local-env/\n<!-- uw-harness:todo local-env -->\n\n`compose.yaml` and the Makefile targets were added by the harness build on 2026-11-01. They are tested on macOS with Docker Desktop.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3.10 (pinned in `.python-version`, used by CI). `make setup` uses [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) to get it when uv is installed, otherwise `python3.10`. Note: the Docker image (`docker/Dockerfile`) uses Python 3.11.\n- Docker with the `docker compose` plugin.\n- System libraries to build and run the requirements: libpq and `pg_config` (psycopg2 is built from source), libmagic (python-magic), cairo (cairosvg), gettext (`compilemessages`). On macOS: `brew install libpq libmagic cairo gettext`.\n- The PostgreSQL client tools (`dropdb`, `createdb`) for `make db-reset`.\n- Port 5432 free on localhost. If another PostgreSQL uses it, stop it: tests connect to `localhost:5432` with user, password and database `taiga` (`tests/config.py`).\n\n## First run\n\n```bash\nmake setup     # .venv, requirements, git hook, PostgreSQL, migrations\nmake db-reset  # optional: admin user (admin/123123), Scrum/Kanban templates, sample data\nmake dev       # API on http://localhost:8000/api/v1/, Django admin on /admin/\n```\n\n`make dev` copies `settings/config.py.dev.example` to `settings/config.py` when the file does not exist (it is in `.gitignore`) and starts `manage.py runserver` with `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=settings.config`. Edit `settings/config.py` for local overrides.\n\nWithout `settings/config.py`, `manage.py` uses `settings.common`. It connects to the same database (`127.0.0.1`, `taiga/taiga`), so `regenerate.sh` and `manage.py` commands work with the compose database.\n\n## Daily run\n\n```bash\nmake dev          # starts PostgreSQL if needed, then the API\nmake check-fast   # lint + unit tests, about 30 seconds with a warm test database\nmake check        # full gate, same as CI (about 15 minutes)\n```\n\nRun one test file or one test:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_slug.py\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/test_userstories.py -k bulk --reuse-db\n```\n\n`--reuse-db` keeps the `test_taiga` database between runs and saves the migration time. Django still applies new migrations to it. Trap: transactional tests (for example in `tests/unit`) flush all tables when they end, which also deletes rows created by data migrations, such as the system users that `taiga/hooks` needs. If a test fails with `DoesNotExist` on data you did not create, run it again with `--create-db`. `make test` and `make check` always use `--create-db`.\n\n## Async work (Celery) and events\n\nBy default `settings/common.py` sets `CELERY_ENABLED = False` (tasks run inline) and uses the PostgreSQL events backend (`taiga.events.backends.postgresql`). You do not need RabbitMQ for normal development.\n\nTo try Celery: start RabbitMQ with `docker compose --profile async up -d`, set `CELERY_ENABLED = True` and `CELERY_BROKER_URL = \"amqp://taiga:taiga@localhost:5672/taiga\"` in `settings/config.py`, then run `make worker`.\n\nThe real-time service (taiga-events) and the web front end are in other repositories.\n\n## Reset\n\n- `make db-reset` drops and recreates the `taiga` database and loads sample data. It destroys local data.\n- `make db-down` stops the containers. The data stays in the `postgres-data` volume.\n- `docker compose down -v` also deletes the volume (all local data and the test database).\n\n## Debug\n\n- Logs: `settings/common.py` `LOGGING` sends the `taiga` logger (level DEBUG) to the console, so `make dev` prints them. Request errors go to `django.request`.\n- Breakpoints: add `breakpoint()` in the code. With `make dev` the prompt opens in the same terminal. With pytest, add `-s`, or use `.venv/bin/pytest --pdb` to stop at the first failure.\n- Data: `.venv/bin/python manage.py shell` or `.venv/bin/python manage.py dbshell`, or `docker compose exec postgres psql -U taiga taiga`.\n- Emails: the dev settings print emails to the console (Django console backend from `settings/common.py`).\n\n## Common problems\n\n- `pg_config executable not found` during `make setup`: install libpq and put its `bin` folder on `PATH` (on macOS `/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin`).\n- `failed to find libmagic`: install libmagic.\n- `password authentication failed for user \"taiga\"`: another PostgreSQL answers on port 5432. Stop it or change its port.\n- Very slow tests: the compose PostgreSQL runs with `fsync=off`. If you use another PostgreSQL, the first test run (database creation and migrations) can take minutes.\n- `pyenv: version '3.10' is not installed`: install Python 3.10 (`pyenv install 3.10` or `uv python install 3.10`), or install uv and run `make setup` again.\nAGENTS.md\nAUTHORS.rst\nCHANGELOG.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncompose.yaml\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nDCOLICENSE\ndocker\ndocs\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nmanage.py\npytest.ini\nREADME.md\nregenerate.sh\nrequirements-contribs.in\nrequirements-contribs.txt\nrequirements-devel.in\nrequirements-devel.txt\nrequirements-tests.txt\nrequirements.in\nrequirements.txt\nscripts\nSECURITY.md\nsettings\nsetup.cfg\ntaiga\ntests\nthankyou.md\ntox.ini","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e94dea2-12e6-4578-b836-e8be0d4edf3c","uuid":"4255f634-d8dd-4a04-a8ce-59a8c6e211a7","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:58:25.673Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Task entry point for taiga-back. Run `make` or `make help` to list targets.\n# All Python commands run from the .venv virtualenv created by `make setup`.\n\nSHELL := /bin/bash\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\nVENV := .venv\nPY := $(VENV)/bin/python\nPYTEST := $(VENV)/bin/pytest\nFLAKE8 := $(VENV)/bin/flake8\n\n# Same coverage command as the CI workflow before the harness.\nCOVERAGE_OMIT := *tests*,*commands*,*migrations*,*admin*,*.jinja,*dashboard*,*settings*,*wsgi*,*questions*,*documents*\n\n# flake8 rules enforced by the gates: syntax errors and invalid comparisons only.\n# The full rule set from setup.cfg (`make lint-full`) reports existing violations\n# in old code, see docs/harness/log.md.\nLINT_GATE_SELECT := E9,F63,F7\n\n.PHONY: help setup venv deps hooks db-up db-down db-migrate db-reset dev worker \\\n        test test-unit lint lint-full migrations-check check-fast check\n\nhelp: ## Show this help\n\t@grep -E '^[a-zA-Z_-]+:.*?## ' $(MAKEFILE_LIST) | \\\n\t\tawk 'BEGIN {FS = \":.*?## \"}; {printf \"  \\033[36m%-17s\\033[0m %s\\n\", $$1, $$2}'\n\nsetup: deps hooks db-up db-migrate ## Install dependencies, install the git hook, start PostgreSQL and apply migrations\n\n$(PY):\n\t@if command -v uv >/dev/null 